-- Bot — bot registration row (token, label, webhook details, collector
-- config). Id<Bot> is first-class for collector dispatch. PascalCase
-- codename: the entity-id and filename both PascalCase, distinct from
-- the lowercase `conversation` (the collector conversation row).
--
-- Static rows: none. Identity (label / description / icon) is
-- registered by defineSystemEntity on the TS side.
--
-- Phase 3d of the system-entities sweep — see
-- workstreams/ts-elimination/briefs/phase-3d-system-entities-wholesale-flip.md.
-- Cross-module reference: `collectorConfig: Maybe (List
-- CollectorEntry)` — `CollectorEntry` is registered by the telegram
-- module's .fenel source (not foundation/std). The `{$named:
-- "CollectorEntry"}` ref resolves through the catalog at validate
-- time (same as `{$named: "Date"}` references everywhere). No
-- ordering constraint on the load loop because resolution is
-- deferred. Three labels need overrides: telegramBotId → "Telegram
-- numeric id", webhookUrl → "Webhook URL", webhookSecret → "Webhook
-- secret" (humanize "Telegram Bot Id" / "Webhook Url" don't carry the
-- intended casing).

@entity
@label "Bot"
@description "Bot registration — token, label, webhook details, collector config. Id<Bot> is first-class for collector dispatch."
@icon "bot"
@fieldLabel "token" "Bot token"
@fieldLabel "telegramBotId" "Telegram numeric id"
@fieldLabel "webhookUrl" "Webhook URL"
Bot = Bot platform: Maybe String token: String telegramBotId: Maybe Int username: Maybe String label: Maybe String enabled: Boolean webhookUrl: Maybe String webhookSecret: Maybe String collectorConfig: Maybe (List CollectorEntry)
